This is where pancake stands: what runs today, where the edges are, and where the
project is going. The code is the truth about the present; the documents linked
below argue the direction without pretending unfinished work is done.

The short version: nothing here is frozen, and nothing here has been reviewed
for security. pancake is not audited, not hardened, and not ready to carry
anything you would mind losing.
[SECURITY.md](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/SECURITY.md)
says that in full, and says how to report a vulnerability privately.
[What you can depend on]($link.page('stability')) says what evidence runs for
each surface and what it leaves open.

```=html
<nav class="cards" aria-label="Project status">
	<a class="card" href="https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/shipped.md">
		<h2>What ships today</h2>
		<p>The short inventory of application APIs, protocol features, codecs, transports, bindings, tools, and examples that exist now.</p>
	</a>
	<a class="card" href="https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/boundaries.md">
		<h2>Known limitations</h2>
		<p>The security, reachability, scale, platform, API, and protocol limits that can change a deployment choice.</p>
	</a>
	<a class="card" href="https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/vision.md">
		<h2>Where it is going</h2>
		<p>The goal is a fully canonical OCapN implementation, proven by interop, with performance held to a measured contract rather than asserted.</p>
	</a>
	<a class="card" href="https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/decisions/README.md">
		<h2>Why the boundaries sit here</h2>
		<p>The accepted decision records: the netlayer contract, the one-parser framing, the C ABI allocation context, the iroh sidecar, and the rest. When a boundary moves, a superseding record explains the move.</p>
	</a>
</nav>
```

The [ladder](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/ladder.md)
orders the climb to 1.0; the
[roadmap](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md) lists
the remaining work. To try the current surface, [start building]($link.page('start')).
